    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35878" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phaenon</span></b> , ōnis,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φαίνων</span> (shining),
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the planet
				Saturn</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quae Stilbon volvat, quae secula Phaenon,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Idyll. 18, 11</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 8, §
			886</span></i>.—In the Gr. acc. Phaenona,
					<i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 8, § 851</span></i>
			(written as Greek, <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D. 2, 20, 52</span></i>). </div>
